# Drafted by Gemini (R11 batch b6), edited. hilda_brom's first conversation.

~ start
set hilda_brom_met
Narrator: Woodsmoke and dried blood drift from her pelts as she tests a broadhead arrow against her thumb.
hilda_brom [neutral]: You walk loud enough to wake every crow to the bog. State your business quick, or step out of my light.
-> menu

~ menu
* Browse her wares -> shop_open
* Ask about her hunting work for the Mayor -> work
* Ask about the Old Ways and the woods -> village
* [Insight DC 14] Ask what quarry she truly fears to track -> bear_ok | bear_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ shop_open
hilda_brom [smile]: Ha, got coin after all? Pick from smoked haunch and winter fur, or hire my boots if you fear the mire.
shop
-> menu

~ work
hilda_brom [neutral]: Somerton pays me to drag runaways back to the Oak of Many Faces. Once a trail is warm, nothing shakes me off.
-> menu

~ village
hilda_brom [smile]: Town folk huddle by bonfires, praying the dark stays out. I keep the Green Queen's custom: take only what bleeds, and leave the heart for the roots.
-> menu

~ bear_ok
Narrator: Her scarred fingers tighten on the bowstring until the sinew creaks, her eyes flicking toward the black treeline.
hilda_brom [afraid]: A great spirit bear walks the deep ridge, calling me to shed my skin and run on four paws. Some nights I want to answer, and that freezes my marrow.
-> menu

~ bear_fail
hilda_brom [sly]: Ha, listen to the new dead playing woodsman! Only thing I fear is a blunt knife and a wet tinderbox.
-> menu
